  "requirement": "When a `{requirements-index}` chapter exists, it MUST list examples as well as requirements, identify each entry's kind, show each example's evidence state, and add one evidence detail subchapter per example. An example definition badge MUST link to its detail page. The detail page MUST link back to the example's anchored definition and to the index; references to the example MUST link to its definition. An example detail page MUST show validation findings when its evidence is missing or invalid.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "IndexPlan creates detail paths for both definition kinds. It lists each kind and evidence state, renders an example-labeled body with links to the anchored definition and index, and shows pending or missing example evidence. The example-index test checks those rows, links, and detail pages.",
